                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Authors: Ayesha Mansoor and Azra Naseem"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "When ChatGPT launched in November 2022, it sparked a ton of discussion about how it "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "would impact teaching and learning, students' cognitive skills, creativity and originality of work. Some even wondered if teachers would be replaced with LLMs in the near future. Faculty members were pretty worried, students were using the tools a lot, and faculty developers weren't sure what their new roles would be (Chuhao et al., 2024). However, in all this debate, one thing was clear: teaching and learning will go through significant changes and faculty must be prepared to adapt. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "We talked with two undergraduate medical faculty members at "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Aga Khan University (AKU)",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "/Pages/home.aspx",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "underline"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " to understand how they use GenAI in their teaching and learning and what medical faculty can do to improve their teaching practices. For this discussion, we invited "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Prof. Simiat Elias",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "/mcea/Pages/biomed-faculty.aspx",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "underline"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", Founding Chair of the Biomedical Sciences Department at Aga Khan University in Nairobi, Kenya and "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Dr Sadia Fatima",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "/mcpk/faculty/Pages/profile.aspx?ProfileID=153&Name=Syeda+Sadia+Fatima",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "underline"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", Associate Professor Department of Biomedical and Biological Sciences Department and Chair of the Haile T. Debas Teacher's Academy. The discussion was moderated by "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Azra Naseem",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "/iedpk/faculty/Pages/profile.aspx?ProfileID=29&Name=Azra+Naseem",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "underline"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", Director Blended and Digital Learning, Network of Quality, Teaching and Learning and Senior Instructor Institute for Educational Development. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "attrs": {
                  "level": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "How are faculty using GenAI?"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Recognising the need to adopt digital technologies to improve student learning and pedagogies, Aga Khan University encourages the use of "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "GenAI ",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "/admissions/Documents/policy-use-of-generative-ai.pdf",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "underline"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "tools in teaching, learning, research and administrative processes. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Both Dr Sadia and Dr Simiat mentioned that they are using GenAI in a number of ways to facilitate their teaching and incorporate the use of GenAI tools in student learning. Some of the most common tools they used were ChatGPT, Gemini, Gamma, DALL.E and Copilot, which helped them save time on tasks that otherwise took hours to do. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Some of the examples of how they are using GenAI tools are: "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "bullet_list",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "list_item",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "Creating slides"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "list_item",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "Making illustrations"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "list_item",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "Generating questions for a quiz "
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "list_item",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "Summarizing information"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "list_item",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "Generating references "
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "list_item",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "Refining lesson plans "
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "list_item",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "Creating case studies"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "list_item",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "Ideas for formative assessment "
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "They also mentioned that they tasked students to create a learning resource using ChatGPT 3.0 and then compare it to the resources given by her. This class discussion, which took place in 2023, resulted in students realising that the faculty resource was more thorough and useful. However, since then, ChatGPT and other such LLMs have gone through significant upgrades and are now better equipped and more knowledgeable than when they were initially launched. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Currently, the faculty is also supporting students in using GenAI tools to search literature, analyse data and create infographics and short videos to summarise lengthy resources that are difficult and boring to read each time. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "attrs": {
                  "level": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "How are students using GenAI tools? "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Students are using GenAI for a variety of things, and most are using it multiple times a day. Some of the most common ways are concept explanation, exam preparation, summarization, visualisation of complex concepts, creating diagrams, etc. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "However, students also found that GenAI tends to hallucinate a lot of information."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "attrs": {
                  "level": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Changes to Pedagogy and Assessment "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Monologues are not the way to go!"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Faculty quickly realised that if their assessments could be easily done by ChatGPT and other GenAI tools, then what would be the purpose of assessment? "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Recognising this, Dr Sadia used an ingenious hack - asking ChatGPT! She used the tool to identify different assessment strategies that she could use, which cannot be hacked using a GenAI tool. This included Pecha Kucha, a flipped classroom approach, class discussions and presentations. Similarly, Dr Simiat focused on students being able to critically connect different concepts together, explain them and role-play in class. Her assessments moved from traditional paper writing to critical analysis and critique. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "But that wasn't enough. They also wanted to build their students' critical AI literacy through their courses, so they started creating activities that involved using GenAI tools for class discussions, critiques and debates. They decided that teachers can no longer be the \"Sages on the stage\" and that it's important to responsibly use GenAI tools to improve class engagement. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "They have replaced traditional lectures with class discussions and student-led learning. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "attrs": {
                  "level": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Challenges of using GenAI tools "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Trusting AI blindly! "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The first challenge was, of course, that students can easily access information, so the faculty must rethink their role as facilitators and revise their pedagogy and assessment. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Some of the most common challenges that the faculty encountered were the inaccurate information given by GenAI tools and the lengthy responses. However, improved prompting and continuous learning helped them get better at using the tools and understanding their limitations. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "However, many students continue to over-rely on the information given by these tools and do not verify its accuracy. When most students use these tools to answer questions, the entire class's responses come out very similar. Some students also input confidential data into the GenAI tools. Faculty also tend to overuse the tools especially when they generate assessment questions using these tools. While it's okay to brainstorm questions and ideas for questions directly, using the questions it generates in assignments poses a risk-others may have access to the same questions or may already be prepared for them. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "To address this, awareness raising has to be done amongst both faculty and students. For instance, Dr Sadia spoke to her students, highlighting that they may pass the exam using GenAI, but when they encounter an actual patient and have to do differential diagnosis and recommend tests and treatment, they will struggle because their concepts are not as clear. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "attrs": {
                  "level": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Can GenAI use negatively affect the development of creativity and problem-solving skills? "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Not at all! Students are actually thinking in new and innovative ways. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "GenAI is not affecting students' creativity but, in fact, helping them work together. Through group activities, students are able to build soft skills like better communication, leadership, critical thinking and peer learning. It helps by doing the mundane tasks while letting you focus on the creative and critical thinking aspects. For instance, in Dr Simiat's class, she has made sure that students must interact with GenAI tools and contextualise responses so the answers can't be directly copy-pasted. Similarly, students also use the speech feature to have conversations with GenAI to understand concepts in a language that they understand best. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "attrs": {
                  "level": 1
                },
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Competencies needed by faculty and students "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Practise lifelong learning "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "This technology is here to stay and disrupt the way we teach and learn, so it's important to build faculty capacity and student literacy in these areas: "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "bullet_list",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "list_item",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "Basics of AI and GenAI "
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "list_item",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "Responsible and ethical use of GenAI (privacy, data protection, ownership, etc.)"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "list_item",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "Change in traditional assessments and student learning outcomes"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "list_item",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "content": [
                          {
                            "type": "text",
                            "text": "Critical appraisal and analysis of information "
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Faculty are actively using, learning, and experimenting with these technologies, recognizing the importance of adapting pedagogy and assessments to remain effective and relevant in teaching students in this era. While generic GenAI tools like ChatGPT and DeepSeek should not be used for grading or providing direct feedback to students due to their lack of transparency in the use of user data, they can still be a valuable tool in designing assessments that promote critical thinking."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Although many countries have access to the latest encrypted AI models through licensed, paid versions, there is also the possibility of creating and training your own LLM using open-source APIs, which can be tailored to your students' needs and will be completely encrypted and controlled."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "If you would like to listen to the entire session, you may go to the following "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "link",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cb0aJYQ8KXE",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      },
                      {
                        "type": "underline"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ". "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
